00:33:04,680 --> 00:33:11,560
But even with regular gasoline, used in this demonstration, the flames can shoot out an intimidating 30 yards.

407
00:33:15,240 --> 00:33:20,920
Imagine yourself with somebody on the other end like that, pointing and fire at you.

408
00:33:20,921 --> 00:33:28,260
Fire through the human psyche is probably one of the most agonizing and devastating forms of pain and death that we can go through.

409
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:34,840
So the idea of using it as an assault and aggressive weapon has a tremendous psychological effect on the opponent.

410
00:33:36,660 --> 00:33:45,200
Other incendiaries also gained widespread use in the Second World War, including white phosphorus, or Willie Pete, as it was called.

411
00:33:46,540 --> 00:33:49,620
It was originally implemented in battle as a smokescreen.

412
00:33:49,621 --> 00:33:58,356
It also became used extensively as an incendiary device because white phosphorus chemical, like that, once it was exposed to air, would continue to burn and often

413
00:33:58,357 --> 00:33:59,920
cases was used as an igniter.

414
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:08,380
We also had an incendiary grenade, handheld grenade, that was sold for the purpose as to ignite combustible products.

415
00:34:09,560 --> 00:34:17,660
White phosphorus starts with a white flash of smoke, which ignites at just 86 degrees Fahrenheit, producing fierce yellow flames.

416
00:34:19,620 --> 00:34:23,560
These flames rain molten blobs of phosphorus pentoxide down to earth.

417
00:34:26,380 --> 00:34:29,840
The substance is menacing as it bonds with skin,

418
00:34:30,180 --> 00:34:34,020
charring the flesh and consuming any exposed area until it hits bone.

419
00:34:36,940 --> 00:34:40,140
While the use of white phosphorus against enemies was unnerving,

420
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:45,600
perhaps one of the most devastating uses of fire was in the form of terror bombings.

421
00:34:45,601 --> 00:34:53,120
One of the most destructive was the bombing of Dresden, starting on February 13, 1945.

422
00:34:54,700 --> 00:34:59,840
For three days, Allied forces dropped thousands of tons of incendiary bombs on the city,

423
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:06,000
creating a self-sustaining firestorm that killed nearly 35,000 residents.

