435
00:36:09,061 --> 00:36:15,300
On impact, the payload of flammable liquid would ignite and shoot out of the tail of the bomb.

436
00:36:18,900 --> 00:36:25,900
Developed in World War II and used extensively by both sides, incendiary bombs often contained napalm.

437
00:36:27,460 --> 00:36:33,440
Napalm is gasoline, sometimes mixed with other petroleum fuels, and a thickening agent.

438
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:39,460
This horrific substance which burns hotter and sticks to human flesh

439
00:36:39,461 --> 00:36:45,980
Gained notoriety during the vietnam war when images of napalmed children fueled the anti-war movement

440
00:36:45,981 --> 00:36:50,440
Despite or because of its gruesome qualities

441
00:36:50,441 --> 00:36:55,420
Some argue that napalm is an effective psychological weapon

442
00:36:55,421 --> 00:37:00,059
Well, people are afraid of fire people have directly experienced fire.

443
00:37:00,060 --> 00:37:03,240
They know that it hurts. They know that it burns

444
00:37:03,241 --> 00:37:13,100
So the proposition that somebody is deploying a flamethrower against you or is bombing you with napalm can have a really bad impact on morale.

445
00:37:14,680 --> 00:37:18,340
Due to the ferocity of weapons such as napalm and white phosphorus,

446
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:24,660
the use of incendiary weapons against civilians was banned by the 1980 Protocol of the Geneva Conventions.

447
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:30,680
But the United States didn't sign the protocol.

448
00:37:30,681 --> 00:37:33,520
And the military continues to use these weapons.

449
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:37,140
It claims not to directly target civilians with them.

450
00:37:37,980 --> 00:37:43,720
As recently as 2004, white phosphorus was used in the battle for Fallujah in Iraq

451
00:37:43,721 --> 00:37:48,260
as a smoke screen as well as an incendiary weapon in shake and bake missions.

452
00:37:48,680 --> 00:37:52,320
Fire has been around since the beginning of man as long as we've been using tools.

453
00:37:52,540 --> 00:37:55,400
And although this technology advances and develops,

454
00:37:55,401 --> 00:37:59,580
the idea of using fire as a weapon will probably stay in man's arsenal

