00:37:59,581 --> 00:38:01,940
as long as we're still around as a species.

456
00:38:03,500 --> 00:38:06,800
Fire has a unique ability to evoke our primal fears

457
00:38:06,801 --> 00:38:08,660
and send our adrenaline running.

458
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:11,980
Sometimes, this can be a good thing.

459
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:18,300
The United States dropped approximately 400,000 tons of napalm

460
00:38:18,301 --> 00:38:19,480
during the Vietnam War.

461
00:38:20,140 --> 00:38:23,220
That was nearly one ton for every 100 Vietnamese.

462
00:38:24,420 --> 00:38:27,460
Fire will return on Modern Marvels.

463
00:38:29,580 --> 00:38:33,280
We now return to fire on Modern Marvels.

464
00:38:39,460 --> 00:38:43,880
The intriguing phenomenon of fire never ceases to draw our attention.

465
00:38:45,980 --> 00:38:51,060
No one knows this better than the creative team behind Universal Studios Hollywood theme park.

466
00:38:52,540 --> 00:38:58,520
I think the goal is when you're designing attraction, you want to really physically affect people and you want to emotionally affect people.

467
00:38:58,521 --> 00:39:02,100
and there's nothing like fire to bring out that kind of reaction in our guests.

468
00:39:02,500 --> 00:39:06,140
We have a lot of different attractions here at Universal Studios Hollywood that incorporate fire.

469
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:10,700
On the studio tour, we have Earthquake, where we simulate an 8.0 earthquake on the Richter scale.

470
00:39:11,100 --> 00:39:13,060
Fire plays a very important role in that attraction.

471
00:39:13,220 --> 00:39:16,200
We have the Waterworld attraction, which has a 50-foot ball of fire,

472
00:39:16,520 --> 00:39:18,880
and probably most importantly, the Backdraft attraction,

473
00:39:19,200 --> 00:39:23,180
which puts our guests inside a chemical warehouse and then literally sets the entire room on fire.

474
00:39:23,181 --> 00:39:29,480
The backdraft attraction is the ultimate fantasy of pyromaniacs everywhere

475
00:39:29,481 --> 00:39:33,660
This set here, set three in the backdraft

476
00:39:33,661 --> 00:39:37,760
Is supposed to simulate the big warehouse fire that was in the movie

477
00:39:37,761 --> 00:39:41,280
And what happens is the guests go into the set

478
00:39:41,281 --> 00:39:44,780
Everything is just sitting normal like a normal empty warehouse

479
00:39:44,781 --> 00:39:47,640
And then we start throwing fire at them

480
00:39:47,641 --> 00:39:54,640
The various fires consume 215 cubic feet of natural gas during each show.

481
00:39:54,641 --> 00:39:56,640
They appear to be out of control.

482
00:39:56,641 --> 00:39:59,640
In reality, they are anything but.

483
00:39:59,641 --> 00:40:02,640
Not only is the entire set made of fireproof material,

484
00:40:02,641 --> 00:40:08,640
the show itself has been pre-programmed to keep the fire on a short leash.

485
00:40:08,641 --> 00:40:13,640
We have right operators in here that start the show and are here basically just to observe it.

486
00:40:13,641 --> 00:40:17,640
Once they push the start button, the whole show is out of their hands.

487
00:40:17,641 --> 00:40:21,640
We have show computers and fire computers that run the whole show.

488
00:40:21,641 --> 00:40:26,640
Every effect is timed and set, and it runs the same show every single time.

489
00:40:26,641 --> 00:40:31,640
And with flames reaching temperatures of nearly 1,650 degrees,

490
00:40:31,641 --> 00:40:36,640
safety and maintenance of the attraction is of the utmost importance.

491
00:40:36,641 --> 00:40:41,640
In order to maintain this attraction backdrop,

492
00:40:41,641 --> 00:40:47,640
Our technicians go in every morning and do a thorough inspection of the building.

493
00:40:47,641 --> 00:40:51,640
They make sure everything's properly aligned, it's all clean of debris.

494
00:40:51,641 --> 00:40:55,640
And then they run test shows and make sure that it's all running as it should.

495
00:40:55,641 --> 00:41:00,640
It's Brian Gobelli's job to assure that everything is in proper working order

496
00:41:00,641 --> 00:41:02,640
before the attraction can be opened to the public.

497
00:41:04,640 --> 00:41:07,640
What I'm going to do now is I'm going to test all the fire effects.

498
00:41:07,641 --> 00:41:10,640
We do this on a daily basis.

499
00:41:10,641 --> 00:41:17,640
They have to fully propagate within 10 seconds.

500
00:41:17,641 --> 00:41:19,640
You'll see that one made that.

501
00:41:19,641 --> 00:41:25,640
And this is one of our accumulated effects where we use an accumulator to store a larger amount of gas

502
00:41:25,641 --> 00:41:30,640
and fire it off and make a larger explosion type effect.

503
00:41:30,641 --> 00:41:36,640
We will crawl down here and look at the igniter and see that it's in good working condition.

504
00:41:36,641 --> 00:41:39,640
We have no frays in the ignition cable.

505
00:41:39,641 --> 00:41:43,380
test our burner bars, make sure that they're not falling and haven't moved.

506
00:41:44,520 --> 00:41:49,140
Each effect has its own pilot assembly, with an igniter and a fuel source,

507
00:41:49,540 --> 00:41:51,520
sort of like the one found on your home furnace.

508
00:41:53,420 --> 00:41:59,100
Once the attraction begins, the pre-programmed controller releases the exact amount of fuel for the pilot,

509
00:41:59,720 --> 00:42:01,740
or network of pilots, to ignite.

510
00:42:04,640 --> 00:42:09,600
Depending on the amount of fuel released, the flow rate of the fuel stream and the shape of the dispenser,

511
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:18,880
you'll have a fireball a wall of flames or maybe just a small fire

512
00:42:18,881 --> 00:42:25,720
with all systems in check backdraft is now ready to flare back to life but the

513
00:42:25,721 --> 00:42:29,380
Universal team has harnessed fire in another attraction with an ironic venue

514
00:42:33,920 --> 00:42:38,640
waterworld is a live-action show with actors in close proximity to shooting

515
00:42:38,641 --> 00:42:43,480
flames and exploding fireballs.

516
00:42:43,481 --> 00:42:47,940
Unlike the backdraft attraction, the controller here doesn't have the luxury of sitting back

517
00:42:47,941 --> 00:42:49,020
and enjoying the show.

518
00:42:49,021 --> 00:42:54,160
There's no way you can leave it on fully automatic or you would get in big trouble

519
00:42:54,161 --> 00:42:55,160
in no time.

520
00:42:55,161 --> 00:42:59,400
You know, I might be firing a flame over here and then I have an upper former coming across

521
00:42:59,401 --> 00:43:01,080
the way in a basket.

522
00:43:01,081 --> 00:43:02,580
I have to make sure that she makes it.

523
00:43:02,581 --> 00:43:06,540
If she stops in the middle, then we've got to do something about getting her out.

524
00:43:06,541 --> 00:43:11,540
There's occasions where a jet ski might die, or I might be getting ready to launch the plane,

525
00:43:11,820 --> 00:43:14,860
and maybe a boat has come untied and drifted over in front of it.

526
00:43:16,100 --> 00:43:20,500
Bill Lehman has been working with fire at Universal Studios for more than 20 years.

527
00:43:22,400 --> 00:43:27,480
All of this stuff up here, you could fire this stuff with like two or three little buttons if you had to,

528
00:43:27,580 --> 00:43:30,200
but most all of this built in is all for safety.

529
00:43:30,340 --> 00:43:35,120
All of these lights and all of these indicators and all of these lamps let me know who's where doing what.

530
00:43:36,540 --> 00:43:39,340
Bill has a virtual arsenal of fire tools at his disposal.

531
00:43:40,160 --> 00:43:42,940
Everything from flares to fireballs.

532
00:43:44,040 --> 00:43:45,600
With the push of just one button,

533
00:43:46,580 --> 00:43:49,940
Bill ignites 150 cubic feet of vaporized propane.

534
00:43:50,580 --> 00:43:55,440
The explosion generates massive 30-foot flames and steals the show.

535
00:43:56,900 --> 00:43:59,000
It's scary and it's exciting, you know.

536
00:43:59,120 --> 00:44:02,760
You couldn't sit in this booth for 20 years every single day

537
00:44:02,761 --> 00:44:06,040
and do show after show after show if it wasn't still exciting.

538
00:44:06,041 --> 00:44:08,200
You know, it's very exciting.

539
00:44:09,020 --> 00:44:10,180
No argument there.

540
00:44:10,940 --> 00:44:14,380
Whatever else can be said about fire, it certainly isn't dull.

541
00:44:15,400 --> 00:44:18,080
It's fitting that fire is finally ready for its close-up.

542
00:44:19,220 --> 00:44:23,120
After all, fire, perhaps more than anything else,

543
00:44:23,740 --> 00:44:25,380
stirs our most primal fears,

544
00:44:26,820 --> 00:44:28,080
ignites our fascination,

545
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:33,000
and is the power at the heart of our civilizations and cultures.

546
00:44:36,040 --> 00:44:44,040
The research was top secret.

547
00:44:44,041 --> 00:44:46,040
18 people were injected with plutonium.

548
00:44:46,041 --> 00:44:47,040
It was a mistake.

